 "field_protocol": {
  "source": "docs/data-collection-protocol.md (also live as site/protocol.html)",
  "what_it_is": "The chapter's volunteer data-collection protocol: how to photograph trail features and record the GPS track so the map can place them.",
  "apps": {
   "geo_tracker": "Geo Tracker by Ilya Bogdanovich, free on iPhone and Android. Records the walk as a track file (GPX).",
   "drive": "Google Drive app, signed in with the volunteer's Google account."
  },
  "key_rule": "A phone camera records NO location in photos. The Geo Tracker track is how each photo is placed on the map \u2014 the map matches photos to the track by time, so the phone clock must be on automatic.",
  "before_you_go": [
   "Install Geo Tracker (Ilya Bogdanovich, free, iPhone + Android) and the Google Drive app.",
   "The chapter shares the photos-inbox folder with each volunteer by Google email, with Editor access. Inside it is a subfolder named with the volunteer's photographer code \u2014 their initials (for example, PJM). That is where the photos and track go.",
   "No Google account, or can't use the Drive app: tell the chapter and they will send a simple upload-form link instead."
  ],
  "in_the_field": [
   "Start Geo Tracker recording BEFORE you start walking or photographing. Keep it running the whole walk.",
   "Photograph each thing you find with the phone's regular Camera app \u2014 signs, posts, boardwalks, puncheons, bridges, bollards, benches, kiosks, shelters, campsites, latrines, registers, water sources, anything built or placed on the trail.",
   "For each thing: a front photo, a back photo if there is anything on the back, and a close-up of any text, numbers, or damage. Those get combined into one pin on the map.",
   "Keep the phone's clock on automatic.",
   "If you can't tell what something is, photograph it anyway and note it \u2014 don't guess. It is marked unclassified and sorted out later."
  ],
  "when_you_get_back": [
   "Stop Geo Tracker and save/export the track (a GPX file).",
   "In the Drive app, go to the chapter's photos-inbox folder, then into the subfolder named with your photographer code (your initials). Upload your original photos AND the GPX track file there.",
   "Upload the originals, straight from the Camera app. Do NOT send photos by text, chat, or the share button \u2014 those copies lose the timing information the map needs to place them, and they can't be used.",
   "Don't rename photos."
  ],
  "what_happens_next": "The chapter looks at each photo group and classifies it \u2014 what it is, what condition it's in \u2014 using the classification page. Each thing gets its own number (like ITM-CP-001). A photo that can't be identified is marked unclassified and flagged for a walk-through \u2014 someone goes to look at it in person."
 },
